Description: keybindings marked allowWhenInhibited pass a grab or inhibitor
 While a view switches the keybindings off, labwc 0.9.3 skips every
 keybinding but ToggleKeybinds. ThinFloe's labwc switches them off for an
 X11 keyboard grab (0002, ThinLinc) and for a keyboard shortcuts inhibitor
 (0004, OxuLnk), so with a remote session in front the volume and
 brightness keys went to the remote machine and never changed the local
 volume or backlight.
 .
 A <keybind> with allowWhenInhibited="yes" (a boolean like allowWhenLocked)
 now matches while the bindings are off. A binding without it behaves as
 before. The attribute lets rc.xml stay the one place that says which keys
 pass: thinfloe-compose-labwc-config sets it on the media keys only.
 .
 thinfloe-specific: not proposed for upstream inclusion, see Forwarded below.
Author: ThinFloe maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
